<<~ ahu #/inscription>>
! Art Sigils — Example Zero Inscription

The following source alone carries the portable inscription. Copy both the native TW5 definition and its call, with the blank separator; exclude this meme wrapper. The entire transmitted source occupies **1011 characters**, including its line breaks; a 1,024-character ceiling serves as a portability *target*, not an ideal length.

```tiddlywiki
\procedure art-sigil(worktype:"artwork" subject read imagery:"follow subject and read" treatment:"suit the read" composition:"serve the read" relation:"where meaningful" depiction-scope:"follow worktype and imagery") <<worktype>>: <<subject>>. Read: <<read>>. Imagery: <<imagery>>. Treatment: <<treatment>>. Composition: <<composition>>. Relation: <<relation>>. Depiction scope: <<depiction-scope>>.

<<art-sigil worktype=`concept-art pinboard` subject=`shattered Olympos, Rift of Tempes, Phlegra` read=`artists disagree on routes through a damaged yet passable mountain` imagery=`luminous relief panorama; vellum route correction; charcoal relic; green refuge` treatment=`Tom Patterson and Bernhard Jenny shaded relief; Luka Rejec mythpunk travel; Piranesi/Ian Miller only in dark Phlegra charcoal; varied papers` composition=`dominant panorama above small studies` relation=`redrawn saddle contradicts painted pass; bone or machine?` depiction-scope=`board alone; figures inside studies; no credits or photos`>>
```
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/literal-rendering>>
!! Literal rendering — Inscription null test

This ahu supplies a **hand-derived literal expansion** of the native TW5 single-line procedure. It serves as a test oracle, not a claim that this assistant ran TW5. Paste the procedure declaration and invocation together into a live TiddlyWiki5 v5.4.0+ instance; compare the rendered textual content, allowing for browser whitespace normalization and surrounding tiddler layout. Copy the characters inside the text block, not the enclosing code fences.

!!! A. Explicit Example Zero call — expected output

```text
concept-art pinboard: shattered Olympos, Rift of Tempes, Phlegra. Read: artists disagree on routes through a damaged yet passable mountain. Imagery: luminous relief panorama; vellum route correction; charcoal relic; green refuge. Treatment: Tom Patterson and Bernhard Jenny shaded relief; Luka Rejec mythpunk travel; Piranesi/Ian Miller only in dark Phlegra charcoal; varied papers. Composition: dominant panorama above small studies. Relation: redrawn saddle contradicts painted pass; bone or machine?. Depiction scope: board alone; figures inside studies; no credits or photos.
```

All eight arguments in the Example Zero call carry explicit values. TW5 should therefore never need a default for this case. The `<<...>>` tokens in the definition substitute their matching named call values in textual order; the procedure's period-and-space separators remain literal.

!!! B. Delegated defaults — expected output

```tiddlywiki
<<art-sigil subject=`a distant coast` read=`the unseen seems near`>>
```

```text
artwork: a distant coast. Read: the unseen seems near. Imagery: follow subject and read. Treatment: suit the read. Composition: serve the read. Relation: where meaningful. Depiction scope: follow worktype and imagery.
```

This second probe omits `worktype`, `imagery`, `treatment`, `composition`, `relation` and `depiction-scope`, making the colon/double-quote **declaration** defaults visible in the rendered result. The `=` plus backtick **invocation** values remain plain text, not required printed inscriptions.

!!! C. Null-test boundaries

* The Inscription budget counts definition, two newline separators and invocation only: **1013 characters**. This ahu lives outside that transmitted source.
* Rendering checks literal substitution, parameter order, defaults, and punctuation; it does not test whether a text-to-image model follows the compositional direction.
* Any deliberate backtick payload containing actual double-quote characters should render those characters verbatim. Avoid output-text quotations when testing Midjourney unless visible text belongs to the intended work.
* A failed comparison could indicate TW5 version, definition scope, code-fence copying, unresolved procedure registration, or different whitespace normalization; do not immediately infer a semantic failure of the Art Sigil language.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/bounds>>
!! Reading, paired cartography and representational boundaries

* The `subject` and `read` retain the governing question: which routes actually work across a damaged, still traversable mountain? The explicit `composition` preserves the dominant panorama over smaller studies, and `relation` preserves an observable route contradiction.
* **Tom Patterson and Bernhard Jenny travel as a paired reference**, jointly grounding shaded topographic relief. Their names address the landform study specifically rather than the entire board's mood. **Luka Rejec** influences explorable mythpunk; **Piranesi and Ian Miller** apply only to dark Phlegra charcoal, not the luminous panorama.
* The Folio retains Heinrich Berann's panorama, Imhof, Raisz, Moebius, Doré, Kilian Eng and the rest of the wider artist register. That expanded ancestry need not accompany a portable image-facing Inscription.
* `depiction-scope` preserves the board as the outer image, with any small figures only inside embedded studies; source photographs and artist names never become instructions to print labels on the artwork.
* New-style TW5 named-parameter calls use an equals sign with backtick-delimited values. This v5.4.0+ syntax lets values include apostrophes and double quotes without double-quote *delimiters*. The generic procedure's defaults use ordinary single-quoted strings or an unquoted token; TW5 handles literal substitution, while the receiving AI interprets the art direction.
* Midjourney can treat double-quoted phrases as requests for visible text. Backticks remove the quoted-string delimiters from this transmitted source, but do not guarantee any model's interpretation or suppress actual quotation marks placed *inside* a value.
* The real Olympus relief, aerial and embodied photographs remain external references in the companion Folio; supply them as actual images when the receiving model cannot retrieve URLs.
<<~/ahu>>
